hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"251","When retaliation is taken for wounds: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Talhah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and a man had struck him with a horn - and said: O Prophet of Allah, grant me retaliation. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Wait until you heal. Then he came to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, grant me retaliation. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Wait until you heal. Then he came to him a third time and said: O Prophet of Allah, grant me retaliation, so he granted retaliation. Then the one retaliated against healed, while the leg of the one granted retaliation remained lame, so he said: O Prophet of Allah, my leg is lame, so grant retaliation. He said: Go, retaliation has been granted for you."
"252","[Ibn Abdah] and Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah ... with the same meaning. Ibn al-Sarh said in it: I already told you."
"253","Musaddad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, with his chain, likewise. Abu Dawud said: Ibn Ulayyah transmitted it with a connected chain, from Ayyub, from Amr, from Jabir, and erred in it; the first is more sound."
